# M23 — the explicit transaction removed from the harness's claim-carrying scoped run.
#
# THE HAZARD, MEASURED. `set_config(name, value, true)` is `SET LOCAL`. Issued OUTSIDE an
# explicit transaction block it is scoped to that single statement, and the NEXT statement
# reads the EMPTY STRING. Measured on the emulation as `authenticated`:
#
#     select set_config('request.jwt.claim.sub', '…dead', true);
#     select coalesce(nullif(current_setting('request.jwt.claim.sub', true),''),'<EMPTY>');
#     -- <EMPTY>
#
# whereas the same two statements inside `begin; … rollback;` return the id, and
# `auth.uid()` returns it too.
#
# WHY THAT IS A SECURITY PROPERTY AND NOT A STYLE POINT. Pre-port, a statement with no
# identity RAISED 28000, so a lost `SET LOCAL` announced itself. `auth.uid()` returns NULL
# instead: a claimless read of a protected table returns zero rows and raises nothing. So a
# scoped run that lost its BEGIN would execute every subsequent statement as NOBODY, see
# zero rows everywhere, raise nothing — and PASS. Every denial assertion in the suite would
# become unfailable, which means unproven. This project has already had three separate
# checks invalidated by a `SET LOCAL` that did nothing, which is why `runScopedAs` asserts
# the setting took effect rather than assuming it.
#
# WHAT THE MUTATION DOES. It replaces the opening `begin` with a no-op, leaving the
# `set_config` calls, the server-side assertion and the caller's SQL exactly where they
# were. The assertion is what must fire: the DO block raises ST099 because the claim GUC
# reads back empty, psql exits non-zero, and `runScopedAs` rejects. The named catcher is
# the sentinel integrity assertion, which is the first thing in the suite to take a scoped
# read — and note that it fails as a FAILED TEST rather than a skipped one, which matters
# because a guard that aborts during fixture setup yields SKIPPED tests that no
# `expect-test` can match.
#
# EXPECTATION UNVERIFIED: the gate could not run in the session that registered this (red
# baseline). The underlying measurement above WAS executed.
# PROMOTED from `expect: uncaught`. The gate reported it PROMOTABLE: its named
# catcher now fails when the mutation is applied, so the guard is controlled and
# the registry should say so. The promotion precondition in the old `todo:` line
# (a green integration baseline) is met.
id: M23
title: the opening BEGIN removed from runScopedAs, so SET LOCAL silently does nothing
expect: caught
proves: the scoped-run helper asserts the identity claim TOOK EFFECT instead of assuming it
proves: a lost transaction makes every protected read return 0 rows and raise nothing, so it must fail loudly here
expect-test: every protected table shows exactly 1 sentinel row to the sentinel user and 0 to anyone else

file: tests/integration/support/db.ts
count: 1
@@FIND
    'begin;\n' +
    `select set_config('${CLAIM_SUB_GUC}', :'${SCOPED_UID_VAR}', true);\n` +
@@REPLACE
    'select 1 as no_transaction_here;\n' +
    `select set_config('${CLAIM_SUB_GUC}', :'${SCOPED_UID_VAR}', true);\n` +
@@END
